## How to Deploy to Google Cloud Run

### Option A: Using the PowerShell Script (Windows)
```powershell
.\deploy_cloud_run.ps1 -ProjectId "YOUR_GCP_PROJECT_ID" -ServiceName "ai-code-review-agent" -Region "us-central1"
```

### Option B: Using the Bash Script (Linux/macOS)
```bash
chmod +x deploy_cloud_run.sh
GCP_PROJECT_ID="YOUR_GCP_PROJECT_ID" ./deploy_cloud_run.sh
```

### Option C: Direct gcloud Command
```bash
gcloud run deploy ai-code-review-agent \
  --source . \
  --platform managed \
  --region us-central1 \
  --allow-unauthenticated \
  --no-cpu-throttling \
  --port 8080 \
  --memory 1Gi \
  --cpu 1 \
  --set-env-vars "STORAGE_BACKEND=firestore,APPROVAL_FROM_EMAIL=onboarding@resend.dev"
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Post-Deployment Configuration**:
> 1. Set `APPROVAL_BASE_URL` to `https://<YOUR-SERVICE-URL>/approval`.
> 2. Mount your secrets using Google Secret Manager or Cloud Run environment variables (`GEMINI_API_KEY`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `APPROVAL_RECIPIENT_EMAIL`).
> 3. In GitHub Webhook settings, point the **Payload URL** to `https://<YOUR-SERVICE-URL>/webhook` and set the **Content type** to `application/json`.
